<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n21302" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ībycus</span></b> , i,
			m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἴβυκος</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A Greek lyric poet of Rhegium</i>, <i>celebrated on account of the cranes which he called upon as
				witnesses of his murder</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Tusc.
				4, 33, 71</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Stat. S. 5, 3, 152</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Aus. Idyll. de Hist. 12, 12</span></i>.
			—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A poor man</i>, otherwise unknown, <i><span class="en">Hor. C. 3,
				15, 1</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
